      "clipStartM": 96.47710351149658,
      "clipEndM": 127.89445540499645,
      "derivation": "The framing rule of src/gltf/Framing.h, quoted so the runner can refuse a mismatch rather than trust it. World bounds [-6.1, -0.8, -0.5] to [17.6, 19.8, 0.5], so centre = [5.750000000000001, 9.5, 0.0] and radius = 15.708675946749938 m. yfov = 2*atan(12/50) from a 50 mm lens on a 24 mm sensor height at sensor_fit VERTICAL. distance = radius / sin(yfov/2) / 0.6 = 112.18577945824651, and the eye is centre + (cos20*cos35, sin20, cos20*sin35) * distance. clipStart is distance - radius and clipEnd is distance + radius.",
      "note": "The glTF carries no camera, so the framing rule supplies one. Roll is 0 because the rule sets it: a roll chosen here and nowhere else would make this subject's placement a second determination competing with the rule."
    },
